<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Afrox shows meagre first-half growth.</title>
<headline>Afrox shows meagre first-half growth.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended March 31, 1997</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, historic cost (cts)     33.1	  vs 31.4</p>
<p>    Shr, current cost (cts)	30.3	  vs 28.2</p>
<p>    Div (cts)			  13.0	  vs 11.6</p>
<p>    Attrib income		    92.55	 vs 84.69</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			    152.41	vs 140.41</p>
<p>    Tax				  54.93	 vs 52.38</p>
<p>    Interest paid		    41.46	 vs 34.36</p>
<p>    Historic cost op profit	202.41	vs 184.43</p>
<p>    Additional depreciation	8.54	  vs 9.67</p>
<p>    CCA profit before interest   193.86	vs 174.76</p>
<p>    Outside shareholders'	  4.53	  vs 4.78</p>
<p>    Share of associates'	   0.40 loss   vs 1.44 profit</p>
<p>    Turnover			   1,077.44    vs 946.91</p>
<p>Div payable July 30</p>
<p>on register June 27</p>
<p>Full name: African Oxygen Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters had forecast a consensus EPS of 37.0 cents, with the range 36.1-37.7, and a dividend of 13.7, with the range 13.3-13.9.</p>
<p>The company said it would offer 0.82 new shares for each 100 held in lieu of the cash dividend.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
